   "start_page": 559,
   "summary": "This concluding section of the educational roster for Osaka Prefecture details private secondary youth schools, elementary schools, kindergartens, and miscellaneous vocational schools, including technical, dressmaking, and medical training institutions. It also catalogues specialized schools operated under government ministries other than the Ministry of Education, specifically vocational and youth training institutes run by the Ministries of Communications, Transportation, Home Affairs, and Welfare. The report concludes with prefectural enrollment and faculty totals as of April and November 1946, followed by a reference map of Central Honshu illustrating prefectural boundaries, major cities, and institutions of higher education.",
